<title>LITHUANIA: LATEST SHARE TRADING SUSPENSIONS.</title>
<headline>LATEST SHARE TRADING SUSPENSIONS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of Lithuania's stock exchange said on Monday said was suspending trade in the shares of the following companies:</p>
<p>1. Lithuanian Savings Bank from 24.06.97 until three months. The nominal value of part of the shares will be changed.</p>
<p>2. Klaipedos Nafta from 24.06.97 for three trading sessions for assimilation of issues.</p>
<p>3. Marijampoles Pieno Konservai from 24.06.97-30.06.97, at the issuer's request because of a general meeting of shareholders.</p>
<p>5. Lithuanian Energy from 30.06.97-01.09.97 due to reorganisation of the company.</p>
<p>The board of the stock exchange also decided to renew trading of Endokrininiai Preparatai from 26.06.97.</p>
<p>-- Burton Frierson, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 18</p>
</text>
